"Skill imbalance strikes an Avowed whose unbound authority outgrows a collapsing affixation."
"The System calls it risk of imbalance and loss of skill assignment."
"It ends in an agonizing death or something much worse."
"Non-Artonans feel it as sourceless dread; some Avowed can sense it."
"A knight's authority can hold it in check for a while, like a weighted blanket."
"The fix is re-affixation by the Avowed's home Contract, or next best Contract I on the Mother."
"Skills crack under the strain and must be reasserted deliberately."
